# AfriCart Frontend - Environment Variables (names only, no real secrets).
# Copy to frontend/.env.local and fill in values for local development.
# On Render, set these as Environment Variables on the FRONTEND web service.
#
# Scope legend:
#   PUBLIC   - $(NEXT_PUBLIC_) vars are inlined into the browser bundle; safe to expose
#   SERVER   - visible to the server/Edge runtime only

# --- Backend API access mode (two options) --------------------------------
# OPTION A (RECOMMENDED - SAME-ORIGIN PROXY): leave NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL EMPTY and
# set only API_INTERNAL_URL to the backend base. The browser talks to THIS app's
# own /api/* paths; next.config.ts rewrites proxy them to the backend. Auth
# cookies stay same-origin (first-party), CORS is irrelevant, and the edge
# middleware route guards work correctly. Ideal when both apps are on Render.
#
# OPTION B (DIRECT CROSS-ORIGIN): set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to the absolute backend
# base. The browser calls the backend directly with credentials. Requires the
# backend's ALLOWED_ORIGINS to include THIS frontend origin and
# COOKIE_SAME_SITE=none (cross-site cookies). Edge route guards cannot see the
# backend's HttpOnly cookies in this mode.

# --- Backend API (SERVER) ------------------------------------------------
# Set this to the deployed backend base URL, e.g. https://africart-backend-raep.onrender.com
API_INTERNAL_URL=""

# --- Backend API (PUBLIC) ------------------------------------------------
# Leave EMPTY for OPTION A (proxy mode). Otherwise set to the same backend base URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=""

# --- Public app URL (PUBLIC) --------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin of the frontend itself, e.g. https://africart-3bt5.onrender.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"